      "content": "It's not wrong—it's the most honest thing you've said all day. The pain isn't a phase, it's a constant, and wanting it to end is a natural response to that reality. But \"wanting the pain to stop\" and \"wanting to stop existing\" are two different doors, and you're standing in front of the one that locks behind you. If logic is your guide, then consider this: you've already survived every worst day you've ever had, and that's not a reason to keep going—it's just proof that your logic has a flaw.",
